From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netifd: reconcile parent-owned dynamic interface sets

Publish dynamic children as the desired set of one exact parent, using the
setup-generation token from the preceding change. An omitted child field
leaves that set alone; an empty array retires it. Prepare all names and
configurations before mutation, reject static or foreign-owned names, and
retain legacy add_dynamic callers.

Own children through the native interface/vlist lifecycle. Retire them on
parent link loss, teardown or destruction; detach parent pointers before
callbacks can observe a dying owner. A rejected child set must not suppress
a valid parent lease, and redefined children cancel pending old removal.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

